# Civic AI Club — how we work in this repo

This repository is **standalone**: `CivicAIClub/case-f-project-pomfret`. All paths are relative to the repo root. Club projects each live in their own repo; the old monorepo (`Civic-AI-Github-Repository`) is archived and must not be edited.

The developers are high school students learning collaborative coding. Prefer clarity over cleverness. If you generate code the developer cannot explain, say so and summarize what it does in plain English.

## Git rules (non-negotiable)

- **Never push to `main`.** Always work on a branch and open a pull request. Merging requires one approving review.
- **Branch names:** `feature/<short-description>`, `fix/<short-description>`, or `chore/<short-description>`. Lowercase, hyphens, no spaces.
- **Never commit secrets.** No API keys, tokens, or `.env` files. If a developer pastes a real credential into a file, stop and tell them. Every environment variable gets a placeholder line in `.env.example`.
- Small, frequent commits with plain-English messages.
- Pull requests use the template in `.github/pull_request_template.md`.

## Where things live

- Beginner Git walkthrough, common fixes, and the club-wide repository list: **https://github.com/CivicAIClub/docs/blob/main/developer-onboarding.md**. Reference it for any Git, branching, PR, or merge-conflict question instead of improvising.
- Project context for this repo: `README.md` and `.cursor/rules/case-f-project-pomfret.mdc`.
